# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Secrets — must never be committed (presubmit also blocks these)
.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets/

# The static Linux binary images.yml cross-compiles into the builder image's
# build context — a build artifact, never committed.
docker/workers/cloister-worker
docker/toolchains/*/cloister-worker
docker/workbench/cloister-workbench
docker/workbench/cloister-git-proxy

# Python bytecode from models/ build+eval tooling (qualify.py).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Decrypted traffic captures from the jailed-claude proxy
# (docs/JAILED_CLAUDE.md).  A capture is a plaintext dump of everything the
# harness sent — including the Authorization header on every request — and a
# TLS keylog decrypts any capture taken beside it.  These are short-lived
# diagnostics the operator switches on to answer one question, never an audit
# log and never committed; the durable record of agent actions is the state
# service's trail.  Listed here before the first capture exists, because the
# entry that gets added after the leak is the one that was needed before it.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
# ...and the ring buffer's segments.  `tcpdump -C -W` appends an index to the
# name it was given (claudeplain.pcap0, .pcap1, ...), which the two patterns
# above do NOT match — so every file the tap actually produces would have
# been committable.  The capture is segmented precisely so an overnight run
# does not become one unopenable multi-gigabyte file, which means the indexed
# names are the normal case, not the exception.
*.pcap[0-9]*
*.pcapng[0-9]*
*.har
*.flow
*.flows
*.keylog
captures/

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local content:
notingithub